---
import Base from "../layouts/BackMatterLayout.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy — Matt Riley" description="The short version of how matt-riley.dev handles privacy.">
  <article class="back-matter">
    <a href="/">← Back to matt-riley.dev</a>
    <h1>Privacy, without the fog.</h1>
    <p>This site is a static personal site. It does not ask for your name, email, or anything else.</p>
    <section aria-labelledby="stored-heading">
      <h2 id="stored-heading"><span class="mono">01</span> What is stored</h2>
      <p>The main collection's toolbox and examples keep their state only for the current page visit. They do not save your choices, scan a repository, or send questions to a model.</p>
      <p>The separate comparison archive uses browser localStorage for Lights, Cat, Sound and Gallery/Catalogue settings, plus a return marker if you choose to leave one. Those archive values are not sent to this site's server.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="collection-heading">
      <h2 id="collection-heading"><span class="mono">02</span> What is not collected</h2>
      <p>There is no analytics tracker, account system, contact form, or server side visitor profile on this site.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare hosts the static site and processes ordinary requests, including network information needed to serve it. That hosting is separate from the interactive examples, which run in your browser.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="links-heading">
      <h2 id="links-heading"><span class="mono">03</span> External links</h2>
      <p>Links to GitHub and mattriley.tools leave this site and have their own policies. The linked projects are separate software; their data handling is not determined by these demonstrations.</p>
    </section>
    <p class="back-matter__updated mono">Last updated: 13 November 2026</p>
  </article>
</Base>
